250554,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgyNTA1NTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8250554?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqla-tester","html_url":"https://github.com/sqla-tester","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqla-tester/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqla-tester/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqla-tester/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqla-tester/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqla-tester/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqla-tester/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqla-tester/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqla-tester/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqla-tester/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1546515807","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/9777#issuecomment-1546515807","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/9777","id":1546515807,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCX5JB85cLfVf","user":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-05-13T03:47:52Z","updated_at":"2023-05-13T03:47:52Z","body":"to be clear the theory is:\r\n\r\n\"concurrency because we are creating a thread-shared AliasedClass on the fly -> race condition -> something goes wrong in the AliasedClass -> adapter returns None -> None gets sent to select() -> error\"\r\n\r\nthe parts I can't reproduce are \"something goes wrong in the AliasedClass / adapter returns None\", but it seems reasonable this is where the issue might be since the issue seems to be under high threaded concurrency and is non-deterministic.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1546515807/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1546678494","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/9777#issuecomment-1546678494","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/9777","id":1546678494,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCX5JB85cMHDe","user":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-05-13T15:03:59Z","updated_at":"2023-05-13T15:03:59Z","body":"OK if I substitute the \"None\" in 1.4 we get the same error, that is:\r\n\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/strategies.py b/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/strategies.py\r\nindex 770320794d..6582812f24 100644\r\n--- a/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/strategies.py\r\n+++ b/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/strategies.py\r\n@@ -206,6 +206,7 @@ class ColumnLoader(LoaderStrategy):\r\n                         return\r\n                 else:\r\n                     c = adapter.columns[c]\r\n+                    c = None\r\n \r\n             compile_state._append_dedupe_col_collection(c, column_collection)\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nthen run a simple test\r\n\r\n```py\r\nimport random\r\nimport time\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import *\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.hybrid import hybrid_property\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import *\r\nBase = declarative_base()\r\n\r\n\r\nclass A(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = 'a'\r\n\r\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\r\n    data = Column(String)\r\n    bs = relationship(\"B\", lazy=\"joined\")\r\n\r\n\r\nclass B(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = 'b'\r\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\r\n    a_id = Column(ForeignKey(\"a.id\"))\r\n    data = Column(String)\r\n\r\ne = create_engine(\"sqlite://\", echo=True, query_cache_size=0)\r\nBase.metadata.create_all(e)\r\n\r\ns = Session(e)\r\nq1 = select(A)\r\nq2 = select(A).where(A.data =='x')\r\n\r\ns.execute(q1)\r\n\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nwe get the same stack trace under 1.4. \r\n\r\n```\r\nFile \"/home/classic/dev/sqlalchemy/lib/sqlalchemy/sql/selectable.py\", line 4394, in __init__\r\n    self.froms = self._get_froms(statement)\r\n                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\r\n  File \"/home/classic/dev/sqlalchemy/lib/sqlalchemy/sql/selectable.py\", line 4475, in _get_froms\r\n    [\r\n  File \"/home/classic/dev/sqlalchemy/lib/sqlalchemy/sql/selectable.py\", line 4476, in <listcomp>\r\n    element._from_objects\r\nAttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute '_from_objects'\r\n```\r\n\r\nwhich means this is *not* happening in 1.4 and something is happening in 2.0, suggesting there might be some new race conditions in AliasedClass itself.   By removing the AliasedClass \"caching\" thing from joinedloader we are sidestepping that issue.  ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1546678494/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1546749283","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/9777#issuecomment-1546749283","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/9777","id":1546749283,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCX5JB85cMYVj","user":{"login":"ejlangev","id":718430,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxODQzMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/718430?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ejlangev","html_url":"https://github.com/ejlangev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ejlangev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ejlangev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ejlangev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ejlangev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ejlangev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ejlangev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ejlangev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ejlangev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ejlangev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-05-13T21:03:12Z","updated_at":"2023-05-13T21:03:12Z","body":"I think I see a possible issue in this codeblock:\r\n\r\n```python\r\n        key = (\"joinedloader_ac\", self)\r\n\r\n        if key not in context.attributes:\r\n            context.attributes[key] = idx = 0\r\n        else:\r\n            context.attributes[key] = idx = context.attributes[key] + 1\r\n\r\n        if idx >= len(self._aliased_class_pool):\r\n            to_adapt = orm_util.AliasedClass(\r\n                self.mapper,\r\n                alias=alt_selectable._anonymous_fromclause(flat=True)\r\n                if alt_selectable is not None\r\n                else None,\r\n                flat=True,\r\n                use_mapper_path=True,\r\n            )\r\n\r\n            # load up the .columns collection on the Alias() before\r\n            # the object becomes shared among threads.  this prevents\r\n            # races for column identities.\r\n            inspect(to_adapt).selectable.c\r\n            self._aliased_class_pool.append(to_adapt)\r\n\r\n        return self._aliased_class_pool[idx]\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf two threads are executing at once it isn't safe to use the length of the list to determine whether to add an aliased class to the pool. The issue I think is the check `if idx >= len(self._aliased_class_pool)`. Imagine we have 2 threads executing this with the following sequencing:\r\n\r\n1. Thread 1 enters this method for the first time and sets `context.attributes[key] = idx = 0`, it now has idx=0 and `self._aliased_class_pool` is `[]`\r\n2. Thread 1 pauses after settings `context.attributes[key] = idx = 0` but _before_ checking `if idx >= len(self._aliased_class_pool)`\r\n3. Thread 2 stars executing this method and sets ` context.attributes[key] = idx = context.attributes[key] + 1`, it now has idx=0 and `self._aliased_class_pool` is `[]`.\r\n4. Thread 2 checks if `idx >= len(self._aliased_class_pool)` and it is so it sets appends `to_adapt` into `self._aliased_class_pool`.\r\n5. This is where things go wrong, because at the end of the method Thread 2 tries to return `self._aliased_class_pool[1]` but that is `None` because Thread 1 hasn't appended yet. This is the start of the issue.\r\n6. Thread 1 wakes up, `self._aliased_class_pool` has a single object in it put there by Thread 2. Thread 1 has `idx=0` and checks ` if idx >= len(self._aliased_class_pool):` and it isn't so Thread 1 skips that if block and returns the aliased class instance put there by Thread 2.\r\n\r\nAfter this things are broken for all subsequent threads using whatever object this method is defined on because there is a disparity between the cached value of `context.attributes[key]` and `len(self._aliased_class_pool)`. When thread 3 comes in it will also return `None` because it sets `idx=2`, inserts the next object into `self._aliased_class_pool` but it has one less element than it should because Thread 1 never inserted anything due to the race condition. This will cause Thread 3 and any subsequent threads to return `None` despite them each adding an element into `self._aliased_class_pool`.\r\n\r\nDoes this make sense?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1546749283/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ejlangev","id":718430,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxODQzMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/718430?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ejlangev","html_url":"https://github.com/ejlangev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ejlangev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ejlangev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ejlangev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ejlangev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ejlangev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ejlangev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ejlangev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ejlangev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ejlangev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1546751976","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/9777#issuecomment-1546751976","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/9777","id":1546751976,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCX5JB85cMY_o","user":{"login":"CaselIT","id":16175304,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTc1MzA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16175304?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT","html_url":"https://github.com/CaselIT","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-05-13T21:22:53Z","updated_at":"2023-05-13T21:22:53Z","body":"I don't think that's the issue since step 5 would result in an index error, not in a None.\r\n\r\nIn any case the proposed fix is removing that part","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1546751976/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"CaselIT","id":16175304,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTc1MzA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16175304?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT","html_url":"https://github.com/CaselIT","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaselIT/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1546794661","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/9777#issuecomment-1546794661","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/9777","id":1546794661,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCX5JB85cMjal","user":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-05-14T02:58:33Z","updated_at":"2023-05-14T02:58:44Z","body":"> I think I see a possible issue in this codeblock:\r\n\r\nthe code in question has been unchanged since at least version 1.3.x - it's nearly six years old.   however, only in version 2.0 are we suddenly getting reports of this issue.  therefore I think it's more likely the race condition is specific to the AliasedClass object or its internal structures, since more has changed on that end.   so I'm not looking at race conditions in that specific code.   the change however is such that the AliasedClass object is no longer shared with other requests in any case and remains local to a single compilation.    I'd prefer to kind of know exactly what's going on that we're getting None in a clause adaption, but I'd have to spend the time digging into that logic as it is not shallow.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1546794661/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users