"events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ppsmilesi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ppsmilesi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-09-24T23:04:43Z","updated_at":"2024-09-25T07:00:28Z","body":"@zzzeek I am not sure I can help you with the resolution of this issue resolution but I would like to let you know that I am still facing it on `1.4.54`:\r\n`AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute '_from_objects'`\r\nIn other cases, I get a similar one:\r\n`AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute '_annotations'`\r\n\r\nI have tried to update to `2.0.35` and I don't get the error but the `joinedload` is simply not applied...\r\n\r\nAs a workaround for now, I am just using another eager loading strategy when I need it.\r\n\r\nThis is really weird because it only occurs when eager loading a specific model, and central to the codebase. The issue has started when I modified all the models to ihnerite from an abtract class (`__abstract__`) that is based on `Base = declarative_base(...)`.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/2372540068/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ppsmilesi","id":152861132,"node_id":"U_kgDOCRx5zA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/152861132?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ppsmilesi","html_url":"https://github.com/ppsmilesi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ppsmilesi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ppsmilesi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ppsmilesi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ppsmilesi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ppsmilesi/subscriptio